==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|leggja}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*lagjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɛcːa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛcːa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|lagði|lagt}}

# {{label|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[lay]], to [[put]]{{jump|is|lay|d|s}}
#: {{ux|is|'''Leggðu''' bókina niður.|'''Put''' the book down.}}
# {{label|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[lay]] (stones, tiles, a road), to [[pave]]{{jump|is|build|s}}
#: ''Að '''leggja''' hellur.''
#:: To '''pave'''.
#: ''Að '''leggja''' veg.''
#:: To '''pave''' a road.
# {{label|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[jab]], [[thrust]]{{jump|is|thrust|d|s}}
# {{label|is|ambitransitive|governs the dative}} to [[park]] (a [[vehicle]]){{jump|is|park|s}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég kann ekki að '''leggja'''.|I don't know how to '''park'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hvernig gekk að '''leggja''' bílnum?|How did '''parking''' the car go?}}
# {{label|is|impersonal|with dative}} to cover with ice, freeze over
#: {{ux|is|Tjörnina '''lagði'''.|The lake '''froze over'''.}}
# {{label|is|impersonal|with dative|of smoke, smell, etc.}} to [[waft]] (over an area, room, etc.)
#: {{ux|is|Reykinn '''lagði''' um húsið.|The smoke '''filled''' the house.}}

